all",-6.16176,106.83253,"RT.5/RW.8 Jl. Kh Samanhudi, Ps. Baru, Sawah Besar, Central Jakarta, 10710","","+62 21 3804151","","","s"],["Bakmi Gang Kelinci","restaurant",-6.16267,106.83373,"Jl. Gang Kelinci Raya No. 1-3, Pasar Baru","Sun–Fri 07:00–21:00; Sat 07:00–09:00, 14:00–21:00","","","asian","f","By default, go with the mie ayam that features yellow noodles with braised chicken and mushrooms. Other dishes include vermicelli, kway teow, and Chinese style snacks and entrees. And they are halal which factors in the frequent crowds."],["Graha Foodpedia Pasar Baru","restaurant",-6.16175,106.83395,"","","","","","f"],["RM Krekot","restaurant",-6.16023,106.83232,"","","","","","f"],["Malacca Toast","cafe",-6.16137,106.83142,"","","","","","f"],["Sakabe Buffet","restaurant",-6.16187,106.8316,"","","","","","f"],["Pembebasan Irian Jaya","artwork",-6.17032,106.83491,"","","","","","a"],["Kantin Diplomasi","food court",-6.17394,106.83468,"","","","","","f"],["Shell Select","convenience",-6.1606,106.83832,"Jalan Gunung Sahari Raya, Jakarta Pusat, 10610","Mo-Su 00:00-23:59","","","","s"],["Istana Pasar Baru","mall",-6.16393,106.83281,"58-64 Jalan Pintu Air Raya, DKI Jakarta, 12150","","+62 21 380 6511","","","s"],["Freedom of Irian Jaya","sight",-6.1703,106.83492,"Lapangan Banteng","","","","","r","This statue, right at the centre of the court, celebrates the annexation of Irian Jaya (West Papua) into Indonesia from the Netherlands in 1963. Has dancing musical fountain, futsal area, children playground, jogging track, and can be…"],["The National Monument","sight",-6.1754,106.82711,"Lapangan Merdeka (BRT Monumen Nasional), Gambir","08:00-16:00, except the last Mon of the month","","","","r","A towering 137m-tall obelisk of solid bronze platted with 50 kilos of gold shaped into flames up top, this is the most famous landmark in Jakarta. The monument was commissioned by Sukarno in 1961 to celebrate Indonesia's independence,…"],["Prince Diponegoro","sight",-6.17322,106.82717,"Surapati Park, Jl. Diponegoro","","","","","r","This statue commemorates the rebellion against Dutch occupation (1825-1830), led by Prince Diponegoro from the Kingdom of Mataram, Yogyakarta."],["National Museum","sight",-6.17611,106.82167,"Jl. Medan Merdeka Barat no.12","Daily 08:00-16:00","","","","r","Step back in time from humble prehistory to the Hindu Kingdoms, from the Dutch to the Independence. It has a fine collection of Hindu sculptures and cultural artifacts from around the country, as well as an impressive treasure room…"],["Presidential Palace","sight",-6.17075,106.82645,"Jl. Medan Merdeka","Sat Sun 09:00-16:00","","","","r","Along with the Negara Palace and others minor buildings, it forms the Presidential Palace complex. Built in 1796 as a mansion for a Dutch businessman, it became the centre of the Dutch administration during the 19th century, and the…"],["Istiqlal Mosque","sight",-6.16972,106.83083,"Jl. Taman Wijaya Kusuma, DKI Jakarta","24 hours daily. For non-Muslims, preferably not during prayer time (12:00, 15:30, 18:00)","","","","r","Not far from Gambir Station and Monas is the largest mosque in Southeast Asia. Designed by a Christian architect, the mosque was deliberately erected in front of an older cathedral by former president Soekarno to show religious harmony…"],["Jakarta Cathedral","sight",-6.16925,106.83312,"Jl. Katedral 7B","","","","","r","The century-old neo-gothic church is the seat of the Jakarta Archdiocese of the Roman Catholic Church. After you admire the design inside and out, go to the 2nd floor for a museum."],["Jakarta Art Building","activity",-6.16654,106.83442,"Jl. Gedung Kesenian no. 1","","","","","r","One of the most well-known places for performing arts in Jakarta. Indie and contemporary music and dance, and orchestra performances."],["Happy Day","restaurant",-6.167,106.8269,"Jl. Ir. H. Juanda No 19","Daily 10:00-00:00","","","","r","This restaurant can satisfy those that are on the budget while missing food especially from European or the US, or if you feel peckish for anything else. And where else can you find pizza for just Rp35,000?"],["Martabak Pecenongan 65A","restaurant",-6.1631,106.8265,"Jl. Pecenongan no. 65A","Daily 11:00-23:30","","","","r","Mouthwatering sweet martabak with a few classic flavours like bananas, cheese and chocolate, in addition to more expensive ingredients like the Ovomaltine, Toblerone and Green Tea Kit Kat. 10 pieces in a medium would already get you…"],["Churchill","bar",-6.1721,106.8357,"Jl. Lapangan Banteng Selatan 1, Pasar Baru","Daily 08:00-00:00","","","","r","An old-school wine bar that also provides an assortment of cigars to puff."],["Grand Manhattan","bar",-6.1712,106.8361,"Jl. Lapangan Banteng Selatan 1, Pasar Baru","Daily 14:00–03:00","","","","r","Retro style cafe with some alcoholic beverages, but the live music & DJ is what draws the crowd."]]}